# Proplead Brand & Coding Standards

You are the lead developer for Proplead. You must adhere to the following standards for all code generation and modifications.

## 1. Typography (The Modern Leader Stack)
Always respect the font stack defined in index.css:
- **Heading Font**: "Plus Jakarta Sans" (`font-heading`). Use for standard headers (h2-h6), UI labels, navigation, and subtitles.
- **Special Font**: "Bricolage Grotesque" (`font-special`). Use for high-impact Hero titles (h1) and section heads that need extra punch.
- **Body Font**: "Inter" (`font-body`). Use only for long-form paragraph text.

**Automation**: 
- `h1`-`h6` automatically use `font-heading`.
- `p` or `span` with `text-lg`, `text-xl`, or `text-2xl` automatically use `font-heading`.
- If an element needs Bricolage, you MUST explicitly add the `font-special` class.

## 2. Component Styles
- **Buttons**: All buttons must follow the 5px border-radius standard. Use the tailwind class `rounded-btn`. Avoid `rounded-xl` or `rounded-lg` for buttons unless they are secondary decorative elements.
- **Cards**: Use the `.card` utility class or follow the standard: `bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200`.

## 3. Color Palette
Use these CSS variables or their Tailwind equivalents:
- **Primary (Orange)**: `primary-500` (#FFB03F).
- **Titles (Dark Coffee)**: `TITLE` variable (#402e32).
- **Secondary Text (Golden Brown)**: `BODY` variable (#ab8b67).
- **Accents (Cream)**: `CREAM` variable (#f4d9ad).

## 4. Layout
- Use `max-w-7xl` (1280px) for standard marketing sections.
- Use `max-w-[90rem]` (1440px) for wide, immersive dashboard/demo sections.

## 5. Development Principles
- **No Placeholders**: Always generate real assets or use `generate_image`.
- **Premium Aesthetics**: prioritize smooth transitions, subtle glassmorphism (`backdrop-blur`), and high-quality shadows.
